mutant: m064_relay_cursor_per_block
target: internal/ingest/hot.go
failure-mode: |
  The hot writer runs the durable batch hook (relay cursor plus verifier
  sync state) only for the batch that closes a block, as the local writer's
  per-block durability did, instead of for every hot batch it commits
  (design §10.4). Batches in the middle of a block commit rows without the
  cursor that covers them. After a leader change the successor resumes
  from an older cursor with older chain state and archives whole events a
  second time.
expected-detection: |
  The layer 3 oracle's duplicates rule (disaggCover) allows only a re-
  archived commit prefix per leader change; whole events archived twice
  fail it. Every full seed has leader crashes between hot batches.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

diff --git a/internal/ingest/hot.go b/internal/ingest/hot.go
--- a/internal/ingest/hot.go
+++ b/internal/ingest/hot.go
@@ -879,7 +879,7 @@
 		hook := h.hook()
 		for i, b := range bs {
 			ops := metastore.NewOpBatch(nil)
-			if hook != nil {
+			if hook != nil && b.start+b.n >= h.cfg.MaxEventsPerBlock {
 				var done func(error)
 				var herr error
 				afterCommit[i], done, herr = hook(ctx, ops, b.last()+1, false, b.prepareValue)
